.TH JITTERENTROPY-OSR 1 2026-09-30 "jitterentropy x.y.z" "User Commands"
.\" groff re-enables hyphenation per paragraph unless HY is 0.
.nr HY 0
.nh
.SH NAME
jitterentropy-osr \- find the oversampling rate a time budget allows the CPU Jitter RNG
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jitterentropy-osr
.I blocks seconds
.RI [ option " ...]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B jitterentropy-osr
searches for the highest oversampling rate at which the CPU Jitter Random
Number Generator still generates a 32 byte block within
.I seconds
on this machine, and prints it to standard output.
.PP
A higher oversampling rate assumes less entropy per measurement and takes
proportionally longer per block. The tool is for a caller that wants the most
conservative rate its time budget allows.
.PP
Each rate is timed by generating
.I blocks
blocks and taking the average.
.I seconds
may be a fraction, such as 0.05. The search starts at the minimum rate of 3,
estimates the answer by linear interpolation and then bisects, up to the
maximum of 20. Its progress is reported on standard error.
.SH OPTIONS
The options set the
.B JENT_*
flag of the same name or field, described in
.BR jent_entropy_collector_alloc (3),
for every collector the search measures. Options are matched by their prefix.
.TP
.B \-\-ntg1
AIS 20/31 NTG.1 compliant operation
.RB ( JENT_NTG1 ).
.TP
.B \-\-force\-fips
FIPS 140 and SP800-90B compliant operation
.RB ( JENT_FORCE_FIPS ).
.TP
.B \-\-disable\-memory\-access
No memory access noise source
.RB ( JENT_DISABLE_MEMORY_ACCESS ).
.TP
.B \-\-disable\-internal\-timer
Never use the internal timer
.RB ( JENT_DISABLE_INTERNAL_TIMER ).
.TP
.B \-\-force\-internal\-timer
Use the internal timer instead of the hardware time stamp
.RB ( JENT_FORCE_INTERNAL_TIMER ).
.TP
.B \-\-all\-caches
Size the memory access region from all data caches
.RB ( JENT_CACHE_ALL ).
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-mem " n"
Set the memory access region to 2^(\fIn\fR+9) bytes, with
.I n
from 1 (1 kB) to 20 (512 MB); 0 leaves the size to the library.
.TP
.BI \-\-hloopcnt " n"
Run 2^\fIn\fR hash loop iterations per measurement, with
.I n
from 0 to 7.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when a rate was found and printed. 1 when already the minimum rate takes
longer than
.IR seconds ,
for an invalid argument, and when an initialization, allocation or read
fails during the search.
.SH EXAMPLES
The highest rate that delivers a block within 50 milliseconds, averaged over
100 blocks:
.PP
.EX
jitterentropy-osr 100 0.05
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR jitterentropy-hashtime (1),
.BR jitterentropy-rng (1),
.BR jent_entropy_collector_alloc (3),
.BR jitterentropy (3)
